      { "label": "glue", "text": ". For it is contained by $AB$ and $BE$, and " },
      { "label": "assumption", "text": "$BE$ (is) equal to $BC$" },
      { "label": "glue", "text": "." }
    ],
    "proof_cite": null
  },
  {
    "role": "deduction",
    "text": "And $AD$ (is) the (rectangle contained) by $AC$ and $CB$. For $DC$ (is) equal to $CB$.",
    "assertion": "AD is the rectangle contained by AC and CB",
    "spans": [
      { "label": "glue", "text": "And " },
      { "label": "assertion", "text": "$AD$ (is) the (rectangle contained) by $AC$ and $CB$" },
      { "label": "glue", "text": ". For " },
      { "label": "assumption", "text": "$DC$ (is) equal to $CB$" },
      { "label": "glue", "text": "." }
    ],
    "proof_cite": null
  },
  {
    "role": "deduction",
    "text": "And $DB$ (is) the square on $CB$.",
    "assertion": "DB is the square on CB",
    "spans": [
      { "label": "glue", "text": "And " },
      { "label": "assertion", "text": "$DB$ (is) the square on $CB$" },
      { "label": "glue", "text": "." }
    ],
    "proof_cite": null
  },
  {
    "role": "deduction",
    "text": "Thus, the rectangle contained by $AB$ and $BC$ is equal to the rectangle contained by $AC$ and $CB$, plus the square on $BC$.",
    "assertion": "rectangle AB*BC = rectangle AC*CB + square BC",
    "spans": [
      { "label": "glue", "text": "Thus, " },
      { "label": "assertion", "text": "the rectangle contained by $AB$ and $BC$ is equal to the rectangle contained by $AC$ and $CB$, plus the square on $BC$" },
      { "label": "glue", "text": "." }
    ],
    "proof_cite": null
  },
  {
    "role": "conclusion",
    "text": "Thus, if a straight-line is cut at random, (then) the rectangle contained by the whole (straight-line), and one of the pieces (of the straight-line), is equal to the rectangle contained by (both of) the pieces, and the square on the aforementioned piece. (Which is) the very thing it was required to show."
  }
]

